   "evidence": "Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/PosDef.lean:62 `def PosSemidef (M : Matrix n n R) : Prop := M.IsHermitian \u2227 \u2200 x : n \u2192\u2080 R, ...` \u2014 no `Fintype`/`Finite` on `n`; EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/DataStructures/Matrix/PosSemidef.lean:92 `lemma PosSemidef.of_submatrix_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg ... (h : \u2200 {\u03b9 : Type*} [Fintype \u03b9] (v : \u03b9 \u2192 n) (x : \u03b9 \u2192 R), 0 \u2264 star x \u2b1d\u1d65 (M.submatrix v v *\u1d65 x)) : M.PosSemidef`, documented as \"the arbitrary-index generalisation of `Matrix.PosSemidef.of_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg`\"; the PR's own CovarianceMatrix.lean:63 `covarianceMatrix_comp ... = (covarianceMatrix X \u03bc).submatrix e e` supplies the needed rewrite, and CovarianceMatrix.lean:89 `isHermitian_covarianceMatrix` already has no finiteness hypothesis.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Probability/Moments/CovarianceMatrix.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `[Finite \u03b9]` (and the `Fintype.ofFinite`) and prove it with the repo's own `Matrix.PosSemidef.of_submatrix_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg`: for `v : \u03ba \u2192 \u03b9` with `[Fintype \u03ba]` and `x : \u03ba \u2192 \u211d`, rewrite by `covarianceMatrix_comp` and conclude from `variance_dotProduct (fun k => hX (v k)) x` and `variance_nonneg`. This needs `public import EpsilonEridani.Mathematics.DataStructures.Matrix.PosSemidef`. `ofRandomVector` still applies unchanged.",
   "issue": "`posSemidef_covarianceMatrix` carries `[Finite \u03b9]`, but `Matrix.PosSemidef` is defined with no finiteness on the index type, so the statement is meaningful and true for an arbitrary family: for every finite `v : \u03ba \u2192 \u03b9` the principal submatrix is `covarianceMatrix (X \u2218 v) \u03bc` whose quadratic form is a variance. `isHermitian_covarianceMatrix` in the same file is already stated without finiteness, so `Finite` is the odd one out, and an infinite family (a covariance kernel of a process) is exactly the case this general file should cover.",
